WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.118
Hi, Traveler! In about three minutes,
let’s set up My Roster, so PawPixl knows

2
00:00:04.168 --> 00:00:05.358
exactly who you’ve built.

3
00:00:08.467 --> 00:00:12.907
My Roster is your character list. Build
Lab, Team Lab and your share cards all reed

4
00:00:12.957 --> 00:00:13.339
from it.

5
00:00:16.233 --> 00:00:19.434
Let’s start by hand. Type
a name in the search box

6
00:00:21.367 --> 00:00:25.310
and tap the character to mark them as
owned. That’s it, they’re on your roster.

7
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:32.153
Open edit details to add level,
constellation, talents, weapon and artifacts.

8
00:00:32.203 --> 00:00:36.356
Anything you skip just stays empty, and
you never need an extension for this.

9
00:00:38.367 --> 00:00:43.436
Got lots of characters? A GOOD file fills
them in at once. It’s a small dot J S O N

10
00:00:43.486 --> 00:00:48.494
file listing your characters, weapons and
artifacts, in a format Genshin Optimizer

11
00:00:48.544 --> 00:00:50.159
and many other tools share.

12
00:00:53.233 --> 00:00:57.860
Not sure where to get one? Press Help me
get my file. It walks you through every

13
00:00:57.910 --> 00:00:58.152
step.

14
00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:05.446
One free option is a Chrome extension
called Genshin GOOD Exporter. It’s made by a

15
00:01:05.496 --> 00:01:09.997
third party, not PawPixl or HoYoverse, and
we haven’t security-audited it, so check

16
00:01:10.047 --> 00:01:13.396
its listing, permissions and
reviews, and decide for yourself.

17
00:01:16.267 --> 00:01:20.259
Prefer not to install anything? That’s
completely fine. Adding characters by hand

18
00:01:20.309 --> 00:01:22.904
always works, and so does
filling in from your U I D.

19
00:01:26.267 --> 00:01:30.124
Sign in to HoYoLAB yourself and open your
Genshin Battle Chronicle. PawPixl never

20
00:01:30.174 --> 00:01:33.693
sees your sign-in, and will never ask
for your password, codes or cookies.

21
00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:41.765
Click the extension, check your U I D and
server, and choose Export GOOD JSON. Save

22
00:01:41.815 --> 00:01:43.573
it somewhere easy, like Downloads.

23
00:01:46.267 --> 00:01:50.535
Back in My Roster, press Import and pick
that file. It’s read right here in your

24
00:01:50.585 --> 00:01:52.532
browser, and isn’t uploaded anywhere.

25
00:01:55.133 --> 00:01:59.075
Before anything changes, you get a preview:
what the file found, who’s new, and what

26
00:01:59.125 --> 00:02:01.213
would change for characters
you already have.

27
00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:08.990
Then choose. Add and update uses the file’s
levels, talents, weapons and artifacts,

28
00:02:09.040 --> 00:02:13.127
and keeps your notes and favorites.
Or only add new characters, or cancel.

29
00:02:15.167 --> 00:02:16.278
And there they are.

30
00:02:18.567 --> 00:02:22.418
Open a character, and their weapon and
refinement came across from the file

31
00:02:24.433 --> 00:02:28.238
and under Advanced, every equipped artifact
piece, with its main stat and substats.

32
00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:34.508
One catch: HoYoLAB only shows what
characters are wearing, so spare weapons and

33
00:02:34.558 --> 00:02:38.875
unequipped artifacts aren’t in the file.
Add those by hand, and the Traveler too,

34
00:02:38.925 --> 00:02:39.306
for now.

35
00:02:42.167 --> 00:02:46.514
To update later, just import a fresh file
and you’ll get the same preview. Download

36
00:02:46.564 --> 00:02:49.268
my data saves a backup of
everything you’ve entered.

37
00:02:52.167 --> 00:02:56.963
That’s it! Your roster is ready for Build
Lab, Team Lab and your share cards. Happy

38
00:02:57.013 --> 00:02:58.015
building Traveler!
